course: dictionary
lesson: 10189
title: Reading a timeline
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A timeline is a line that shows events in the order they happened. The earliest event is at one end and the latest is at the other. «A timeline shows events in the order they happened, with equal steps for equal numbers of years.»
explain: Think of a timeline like a ruler. «We put events in order on a timeline, a line where each step stands for the same number of years, like the marks on a ruler.» Check the marks first, so you know how many years each step is worth before you read the events.
explain: A timeline can also be a plan of when things must be done, or the list of newest posts on social media. In history it is the line of events. When you meet the word, check which meaning fits the sentence around it.
fact: A timeline is a line with events marked on it in the order they happened.
fact: Equal steps on a timeline stand for equal amounts of time, like the marks on a ruler.
fact: «On a 1-metre timeline of the last 2,000 years, each centimetre stands for 20 years.»
fact: In maths, a timeline works like a number line, so you can find the years between two events by subtracting.
fact: A timeline can also mean a plan of deadlines, or the list of newest posts on social media.
exercise: What does a timeline show? | The weight of a book | The colour of a map | *The order in which events happened
exercise: On a timeline where each centimetre stands for 20 years, how many years do 5 centimetres stand for? | 20 years | 5 years | *100 years | 25 years
exercise: On a timeline going from left to right, which event happened earliest? | The one in the middle | The one on the far right | *The one on the far left
test: In «On a timeline of Earth's 4.5 billion years squashed into 24 hours», what do the 24 hours stand for? | Midnight | *Earth's whole 4.5 billion years | A single day of human life | Six seconds
test: Your teacher says, «Put these Viking events in order on a timeline.» Which order does a timeline use? | *Earliest to latest | Random | Alphabetical | Biggest to smallest
exam: Which of these best describes a timeline? | *A line or chart of events in the order they happened, with times marked along it | A map showing where rivers flow | A picture of a clock face | A list of random facts with no times
